To generate a table of contents (TOC) automatically in a LaTeX document, you can use the `toc` package and the `\tableofcontents` command. Here's an example:

1. First, add the `toc` package to the preamble of your LaTeX document:

   ```latex
   \documentclass{article}
   \usepackage{toc}
   % other packages and customizations
   \begin{document}
   ```

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command after the `\begin{document}` command, but before the first chapter or section:

   ```latex
   \documentclass{article}
   \usepackage{toc}
   % other packages and customizations
   \begin{document}
   \tableofcontents
   % start of the document content
   \section{Section 1}
   \subsection{Subsection 1.1}
   \section{Section 2}
   \subsection{Subsection 2.1}
   \subsubsection{Subsubsection 2.1.1}
   % ...
   \end{document}
   ```

3. Compile your LaTeX document using a tool like `pdflatex`. The first time you compile, the TOC will be generated based on the sections and subsections in your document.

   If you make changes to your document, you will need to recompile it to update the TOC.

4. The generated TOC will look something like this:

   ```latex
   Contents
   1. Section 1 ............................... 3
     1.1 Subsection 1.1 ....................... 3
   2. Section 2 ............................... 4
     2.1 Subsection 2.1 ....................... 4
       2.1.1 Subsubsection 2.1.1 ............... 4
   ```

Note that the formatting of the TOC may vary depending on your document class and the settings in your LaTeX document. You can customize the TOC further by adjusting the `toc` package options or using other packages like `tocloft` or `titletoc`.

